MEDICAL CORPS -- HEAT EXPOSURE & DEHYDRATION LOG
Sunagakure Medical Division

The chief field hazard of Sand shinobi is not the enemy but the sun. This log
records heat-related casualties and informs the survival syllabus.

Recorded case pattern (this cycle):
- Genin, cross-dune escort: early dehydration, treated with rationed fluids and
  shade rest; returned to duty. Cause: water discipline lapse.
- Chunin, sandstorm exposure: minor heatstroke after prolonged anchoring; full
  recovery. Cause: extended storm delay.
- Recovered caravan traveler (civilian): moderate heat exposure; stabilized and
  returned to the village.

Standing guidance:
- Enforce the water ration policy; most cases trace to its neglect.
- March at dawn and dusk; shade at midday.
- Watch for confusion and cessation of sweating -- signs of severe heatstroke;
  cool and rehydrate at once and evacuate.

Cases are cross-filed to the shinobi's medical record. Maintained by the corps.
